<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Destiny 1 (PS4) CUSA00219 01.29: the cloth time step as a guest patch (FRAME-RATE-INDEPENDENCE-
  20261006.md section 4.2; implementation FRAME-RATE-PHASE1-IMPL-20261006.md). Same format and
  address convention as the launcher's manifest (Address = eboot virtual address + 0x400000);
  `Original` holds the bytes the write replaces, which native/guest_patches.py checks.

  The cloth solve (0x7f0850, every rendered frame) loads a constant 0.0333 s as its step at
  two sites: 0x7f0905 (the flag byte 0x18c6eda clear) and 0x7f090f (the byte set, the shipped
  default, and the frame's time over 1 ms). At 60 frames a second that is cloth at twice its
  speed. Each load becomes `vmovss xmm0, [rdx + 0x192e8]`, the render packet's accepted time,
  the value the engine's own guard at 0x7f08ee compares against 1 ms (that guard, which gives
  dt 0 and sets a pause byte, is kept).

  SCOPE: only with the fixed-clock override on (one tick per rendered frame, so no catch-up
  groups), the emulator's 60 FPS profile. Do not combine it with guest/CUSA00219-native-clock.xml
  or any native-clock configuration: there, every frame of a 2-tick catch-up group carries the
  whole group's accepted time in the packet (the continuation path copies it, 0x590d92, and X5
  publishes it on every frame, 0x7eaf7c), so cloth would integrate up to twice the wall time
  below 60 FPS. That the override gives one tick per frame and no continuation frames is [I]
  (FRAME-CAPS-REMOVED-20261005.md section 5), not checked on the emulator.

  The native loader does not use these bytes. Under D1_FRAME_UNITS=1 it hooks both loads
  (d1_frame_time.c) and gives cloth each frame's own share of its group (frame record +0x08,
  which sums to the group's accepted time); if this manifest was applied first, the hooks
  replace its loads just the same. Findings that depend on this file carry the launcher
  manifest's provenance rule (synthetic_ancestor).
-->
<Patch>
  <Metadata Name="D1 frame units: cloth steps the packet's accepted time, not 1/30 s (fixed-clock override only)"
            isEnabled="true" AppVer="01.29" Author="native-client frame time" PatchVer="1.1">
    <PatchList>
      <!-- 0x7f0905: vmovss xmm0,[rip+0xe61863] (0x1652170 = 0.0333) -> vmovss xmm0,[rdx+0x192e8] -->
      <Line Type="bytes" Address="0xBF0905" Value="c5fa1082e8920100" Original="c5fa10056318e600"/>
      <!-- 0x7f090f: vmovss xmm0,[rip+0xe61859] (0x1652170 = 0.0333) -> vmovss xmm0,[rdx+0x192e8] -->
      <Line Type="bytes" Address="0xBF090F" Value="c5fa1082e8920100" Original="c5fa10055918e600"/>
    </PatchList>
  </Metadata>
</Patch>
